 ## Overview
-Multi-channel surface voxelization is a real-time GPU technique that rasterizes 3D geometry into a uniform voxel grid while simultaneously computing and storing multiple surface attributes (such as albedo, normals, and spherical harmonics coefficients) per voxel [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from binary occupancy voxelization methods by supporting partial occupancy, transparency, and rich multi-channel data in a single pass, albeit at a higher computational cost [S1, unofficial].
